                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 21,
                "quote": "let ensureNotBlocked memberId action (library: Library) : Result<unit, LendingError> ="
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Host/Cli/CommandLine.fs",
                "line": 159,
                "quote": "UseCases.borrow ports m c |> render showBorrow"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The change moves the block decision into Tier 2. `Accounts.ensureNotBlocked` is called from `Loans.borrow`, `Loans.renew` and `Holds.place`. The Tier 4 CLI code that summed fines and payments and compared them to 5.00m is deleted, so a Tier 4 site no longer decides the rule. Tier 3 views (`standing`, `members`) call `Accounts.isBlocked` and do not re-derive it. The CLI only chooses the 'in good standing' or 'blocked' wording. The unchanged `renew` branch in the CLI still loads the store (shown only as diff context). I can't tell what it does with the library, and it is not part of this change.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The change adds no new effect in any tier. The new Tier 2 functions are pure. The new `UseCases.standing` goes through the existing `query ports` path. The change removes a direct `ports.Store.Load()` read from the CLI `borrow` branch, so Tier 4 presentation no longer interleaves a decision with a store read.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The threshold has one definition, `Policy.blockingBalance`. Tier 2 `isBlocked` and the Tier 3 error text in `describeError` both reference it. The duplicate 5.00m literal in the CLI is removed. The refusal and status wording each live in one place. The numbers in the test are test fixtures.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The type-dependent threshold is a Tier 2 rule. `Policy.blockingBalance` now maps member type to an amount, and `Accounts.blockingBalanceOf` and `isBlocked` use it. `MemberBlocked` carries the limit, so the Tier 3 `describeError` only formats the value Tier 2 supplied. It no longer reads Policy itself. No Tier 3 or Tier 4 site re-derives the threshold.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The change is pure rule logic in Tier 1 and Tier 2 plus message formatting. It adds no clock, I/O, persistence or console access and no port bypass.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 22,
                "quote": "|> Option.defaultValue (Policy.blockingBalance Standard)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The per-type amounts exist only in `Policy.blockingBalance`. Every use goes through `blockingBalanceOf` or the limit carried in the error. The decision document is updated to revision 2 in the same change. The unknown-member fallback to Standard references Policy and does not copy a literal, so the fact is still defined once.",
            "score": 2
          }
